# Living Care Record UX (SolenOS)

**The Living Care Record is the product. The AI is almost invisible.**

SolenOS is not an AI chatbot. Caregivers update and understand a care record — they do not converse with an assistant or read how a model thinks.

## After every interaction

Caregiver should think: *SolenOS understood what happened and knows what it still needs.*  
Never: *The AI is showing me how it thinks.*

## Progressive disclosure

Caregiver UI shows **only** the four Living Care Record sections (+ optional original notes). Related observations grow an Active Care Situation.
Engine panels and internal terms are **never rendered** in the caregiver workspace.

## Forbidden in caregiver UI

Internal terms (`ambiguous_extraction`, `partial_signal`, `reasoning_chain`, …), confidence percentages, system-layer dumps. Logs/devtools only.

## Tone

Calm, trustworthy, concise, evidence-based. Context before urgency. Never generic one-list clarifiers for every event type.

## Visual

Care Reality cards — not chatbot bubbles. See [`solenos-visual-language.md`](../../docs/02-product/solenos-visual-language.md).

## Module

`src/lib/living-care-record-ux` · UI: `LivingCareRecordPanel` · ADR-019
